  "description": "Proposed Tree Works\r\r1 ? Red Oak (larger tree)\rReduce over-extended lateral growth within the lower crown by approximately 3?4m and lateral growth within the upper crown by approximately 1?2m, ensuring that growth does not extend beyond the midpoint of the access road. Pruning cuts to be made back to suitable growth points, with reductions tapered into the upper crown. No height reduction is proposed.\r\rRemove the lowest downward-growing branch extending over the road, cutting back to the secondary union approximately 1.5m from the main trunk. Crown lift by removing twiggy growth only to approximately 5m, retaining all other structural limbs.\r\r2 ? Red Oak Trees (smaller trees)\rCrown lift by removing twiggy growth only to approximately 5m, retaining all structural limbs. Remove deadwood where present.",
